From d625b83ccd58540ad20bf127c51943840d085189 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:53:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 28/51] Offer one subtitle menu entry per cached translation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A video translated with several provider profiles used to expose
only the active profile's bilingual track, so switching to another
translation required changing the active profile first.

List every completed cache across all profiles in the playback
resolver and append one subtitle track per translation, labeled
after its profile (e.g. "Bilingual（Google）"), with the active
profile's track on top of the menu. Switching is the regular
subtitle menu flow: picking an entry just prefers that track's
language, which now routes to the self-drawn bilingual rendering
via a case-insensitive "bilingual" prefix match that also covers
the legacy single track.

The post-translation auto-apply now selects the language of the
track that just finished instead of the hard-coded one.
